13. Consideration of a resolution proclaiming April 2025 as Child Abuse
Awareness and Prevention Month.
25 - 128
Resolution Proclaiming April 2025 Child Abuse
Awareness and Prevention Month
Attachments:
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, that this agenda item be approved. The motion
carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
Resolutions
14. Consideration of a resolution approving Wyoming Downs, LLC, to
conduct parimutuel wagering on live horse racing, historic horse
racing and simulcast events at Terry Ranch Business Park, Tract 4,
Laramie County, WY.
25 - 126
Resolution, Wyoming Downs, LLC, Parimutuel
Wagering
Attachments:
Kyle Ridgeway, Wyoming Downs, LLC, said the request is approval for a transfer of
location. He said the license would be used at the current location until construction is
completed at the new location. He said the new location would be state-of-the-art and
bring in additional revenue from out-of-state.
Chairman Malm opened the meeting for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the comment period.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, that this agenda item be approved. The
motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
15. Consideration of a revision of a resolution changing the name
regarding a subdivision permit and plat for Recco Ranch nka Fertig
Ranch (250204-19), situated in the NW1/4 of Sect 11, T14N, R65W of
the 6th PM, Laramie County, WY, original action approved on Feb 4,
2025.
25 - 122
